26669227|body|Berger et al. ONC-2013-01332 (ONC.2013.581) Supplementary Table 4 and 5 legends. Supplementary Table 4. Cell line oncogene genotypes and RIT1 expression data. Expression data was curated from the Cancer Cell Line Encyclopedia (CCLE) (27). Oncogene genotypes shown were previously reported (39, 40) or curated from the CCLE. Cell lines were annotated as  oncogene-negative  if there were no canonical mutations present in the genes listed. Expression from oncogene-negative CCLE lines is shown in Supplementary Figure 4. Supplementary Table 5. Sanger sequencing of lung cancer cell lines. Tabel shows cell lines selected or not selected for cDNA sequencing of RIT1. Oncogene genotypes are as reported (39, 40) or curated from the CCLE (27). 19 cell lines lacking other known oncogene mutations were selected for RIT1 cDNA sequencing ( RIT1 seq ) by Sanger sequencing, in addition to 3 cell lines with known oncogene mutations. A portion of RIT1 (codons 62-108), including the switch II domain, was PCR amplified and Sanger sequenced as described in the Materials and Methods.

